From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 09:28:34 +0200
Subject: net: lantiq: xrx500_phy_fw: drop the dead ret in xrx500_gphy_boot

xrx500_gphy_boot() declares ret, leaves it uninitialised through every
early return, assigns 0 to it on the last line of the body and then
returns the literal 0. The variable has had no reader since the function
stopped relaying reset-control errnos and started driving the GPHY reset
through RCU_RST_REQ directly.

The kernel suppresses -Wunused-but-set-variable by default and W=1 lifts
the suppression, so with CONFIG_WERROR this is a build failure rather
than a warning. Remove the variable and the store.

No functional change.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/xrx500_phy_fw.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/xrx500_phy_fw.c
index 2fed2deb3c73..ecc99d59c8a2 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/xrx500_phy_fw.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/xrx500_phy_fw.c
@@ -176,7 +176,6 @@ static int xrx500_gphy_boot(struct device *dev, struct reset_control *phy_rst,
 			    u32 silicon_id, dma_addr_t dev_addr)
 {
 	int idx;
-	int ret;
 
 	if (!of_machine_is_compatible("intel,xrx500"))
 		return 0;
@@ -235,7 +234,6 @@ static int xrx500_gphy_boot(struct device *dev, struct reset_control *phy_rst,
 		writel(readl(rcu_rst_base) & ~rd, rcu_rst_base);
 		udelay(100);
 	}
-	ret = 0;
 
 	return 0;
 }
